vised edition, ca. 1955-56 printing","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-08-27.damasus-pope-collect","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","retain project j orthography","omit the Lasance comma after Pontificem to match the target"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 439, no. 1887; artifact PDF p. 520","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.sanctoral-damasus-pope-collect"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"The project-created artifact owns the projection while the separately registered Lasance OCR artifact supplies the United States public-domain basis established at registration-number level; the selected project-artifact lines hash to this calendar body.","locator":"project editorial artifact physical lines 48-50; antecedent Lasance OCR rights record","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-08-27.normalized-latin-propers-0bf4adcc","artifact.francis-xavier-lasance.the-new-roman-missal.benziger-revised-1945.new-roman-missal-text-80b34759"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"8be4980dfd10f7a70ea1e0674d51271639d7f187b2013678d884a52f51d1bef5","withheld":false},"name":"Collect","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Gregem tuum, Pastor aeterne, placatus intende: et per beatum Damasum\nSummum Pontificem perpetua protectione custodi; quem totius Ecclesiae\npraestitisti esse pastorem. Per Dominum.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"A lay hand missal of the 1945 revision, printed about 1955-56, not an approved liturgical translation and never an altar book. Its Holy Week is the pre-1955 rite, its sanctoral is not the 1962 sanctoral, and its second and third orations are not those of 1962. It is carried only where a 1962 formulary is the same prayer, and nothing here may be used for recitation.\n\nLeaf n853, printed p. 855, running head `DEC. 11-ST. DAMASUS, POPE`, under `Prayer` in the Mass headed `St. Damasus, Pope, Confessor`. The Latin is the 1962 slot's prayer word for word, differing only by the witness's comma after `Pontificem`. This replaces the Cummiskey 1861 `Exaudi, Domine, preces nostras` row formerly attached here: that pre-1955 book appoints a different Collect on 11 December, while the controlling 1962 Missal and this ca. 1955-56 Lasance printing appoint `Gregem tuum, Pastor` with Damasus's name supplied.","lang":"en","rights":"public-domain","source_id":"edition.francis-xavier-lasance.the-new-roman-missal.benziger-revised-1945","source_label":"The New Roman Missal in Latin and English, revised edition, by F. X. Lasance and Francis Augustine Walsh (New York: Benziger Brothers, 1945), ca. 1955-56 printing (Internet Archive delivery locator fr-lasance-missal-1937; locator mislabelled)","text":"O eternal Shepherd, do Thou look favorably upon Thy flock, which we beseech Thee to guard and keep for evermore through the blessed Damasus, Supreme Pontiff, whom Thou didst choose to be the chief shepherd of the whole Church. Through Our Lord.\n"}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[{"book":"1 Peter","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":5,"first":1,"last":4}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":5,"first":1,"last":4}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":5,"first":1,"last":4}]},"ref":"1 Peter 5:1-4","token":"1Pet","unresolved":null},{"book":"1 Peter","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":5,"first":10,"last":11}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":5,"first":10,"last":11}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":5,"first":10,"last":11}]},"ref":"1 Peter 5:10-11","token":"1Pet","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"la","publication_basis":"unresolved","relatio